course: dictionary
lesson: 963
title: Blubber: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Harp seal pups build a thick layer of fat called blubber before they swim in icy water.» The clues are fat, and icy water. Blubber is the thick layer of fat under the skin of whales, seals and penguins, and it keeps them warm.
explain: «Seals haul out on rocks to rest, warm up and look after pups, and a thick layer of blubber keeps them warm in icy water.» Ask: what word would fit here? Try fat in place of blubber: «a thick layer of fat keeps them warm» still makes sense, so blubber is a kind of fat.
explain: Blubber can also be an informal verb. To blubber means to cry noisily, with tears and sobs. The clue is what the person is doing, such as crying and sobbing. Blubber can also be used unkindly about a person's fat, so do not use it that way.
fact: Blubber is the thick layer of fat under the skin of whales, seals and penguins.
fact: Blubber keeps animals warm in cold water, and it also stores energy.
fact: «The bowhead whale has blubber up to about 50 cm thick.»
fact: Informally, «to blubber» means to cry noisily, often with tears and sobs.
fact: Using blubber to insult a person about their weight is rude and unkind.
exercise: «Harp seal pups build a thick layer of fat called blubber before they swim in icy water.» What is blubber? | A sort of ice that floats | *A thick layer of fat under the skin | A kind of cold, icy water | A small white seal pup
exercise: Ella says, «The baby stopped playing and began to blubber.» What does blubber mean here? | To sleep on a rock | To make a loud splash | To swim very fast | *To cry noisily, with tears and sobs
exercise: «A thick layer of blubber keeps seals warm in icy water.» Why does a seal need blubber? | To help it fly faster | To help it see in the dark | To make it lighter for diving | *To keep warm in cold water
test: «A thick layer of blubber keeps seals warm in icy water.» Which word is closest in meaning to blubber? | pup | rock | water | *fat
test: What does the informal verb «blubber» mean? | To glow in the dark | To rest on the rocks | *To cry noisily, with tears and sobs | To swim under the ice
exam: In «The bowhead whale has blubber up to about 50 cm thick», what does blubber mean? | A noisy whale call | *A thick layer of fat under the skin of a whale, which is a clue from the thickness | A layer of fat under the skin of a whale | Ice that breaks easily
